§ `s 137V(5): the offence`
-- split site (i), both readings: a failure is guilty; no failure is not read as innocent
#ASSERT `s 137V(5) the trustee is guilty of an offence of failing to comply with the register provisions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137V(5) the trustee is guilty of an offence of failing to comply with the register provisions` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137V(5) the penalty on conviction` EQUALS Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000



§ `s 137W(1) to (5): the court's powers`
-- the three conditions of subsection (1) (split site (ii), both readings): all met, the power; any one missing, not covered
#ASSERT `s 137W(1) the court has power to make one or more of the orders listed in the subsection` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137W(1) the court has power to make one or more of the orders listed in the subsection` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137W(1) the court has power to make one or more of the orders listed in the subsection` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137W(1) the court has power to make one or more of the orders listed in the subsection` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137W(2) the order may include ancillary or consequential provisions the court thinks just` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137W(2) the order may include ancillary or consequential provisions the court thinks just` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a sale order carrying the condition, and a buyer who is or would become a substantial unitholder: the sale is barred
#ASSERT `s 137W(3) the sale to the buyer is barred by the court's condition` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137W(3) the sale to the buyer is barred by the court's condition` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137W(3) the sale to the buyer is barred by the court's condition` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137W(3) the sale to the buyer is barred by the court's condition` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4), split site (ii), both readings
#ASSERT `s 137W(4) the Authority may apply to the court for directions on the unsold unit` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137W(4) the Authority may apply to the court for directions on the unsold unit` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137W(5) the court must first satisfy itself that the order would not unfairly prejudice any person` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137W(5) the court must first satisfy itself that the order would not unfairly prejudice any person` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 137W(6): when the court is not to make an order`
-- inadvertence and the failure ought to be excused: the court is not to make (most) orders
#ASSERT `s 137W(6) the court is not to make the order` `s 137W(1)(a) an order restraining the substantial unitholder from disposing of any interest in the units` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137W(6) the court is not to make the order` `s 137W(1)(e) an order directing the sale of any or all of the units` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the carve-out "other than an order restraining the exercise of voting rights": paragraph (c) is not barred
#ASSERT `s 137W(6) the court is not to make the order` `s 137W(1)(c) an order restraining the exercise by any person of any voting or other rights attached to a unit` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- fork register A7: an order that the exercise of voting rights be disregarded is not "an order restraining" it, so it is barred
#ASSERT `s 137W(6) the court is not to make the order` `s 137W(1)(h) an order that any exercise of the voting or other rights attached to units be disregarded` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- either condition missing: the "if" is not met, the text's no (marginal reading (a))
#ASSERT `s 137W(6) the court is not to make the order` `s 137W(1)(a) an order restraining the substantial unitholder from disposing of any interest in the units` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 137W(6) the court is not to make the order` `s 137W(1)(a) an order restraining the substantial unitholder from disposing of any interest in the units` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `s 137W(7) to (10): notice, rescission, contravention and contempt`
#ASSERT `s 137W(7) the court may direct that notice of the application be given or published` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137W(7) the court may direct that notice of the application be given or published` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137W(8) the court may rescind, vary, discharge or suspend the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137W(8) the court may rescind, vary, discharge or suspend the order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137W(9) the person is guilty of an offence of contravening an order of the court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137W(9) the person is guilty of an offence of contravening an order of the court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137W(9) the penalty on conviction` EQUALS Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000
#ASSERT `s 137W(10) subsection (9) does not affect the court's powers in relation to the punishment of contempt` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137W(10) subsection (9) does not affect the court's powers in relation to the punishment of contempt` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the prohibition as a rule: contravening the order is a breach; doing nothing leaves the rule standing
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 137W(9) the person shall not contravene an order of the court` (Individual "the person") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "the person" DOES `s 137W contravene an order of the court made under the section` AT 1
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 137W(9) the person shall not contravene an order of the court` (Individual "the person") AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 5)



§ `s 137X(1): the notice to a member (a power: not covered when a condition is missing)`
-- a trustee, a member, a written notice with a reasonable time
#ASSERT `s 137X(1) the trustee may require the unitholder to give the information` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137X(1)(a) the trustee may require the unitholder to inform it whether the unitholder holds voting units as beneficial owner or as trustee` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not a trustee as section 130(2) reads the word; not a member; not in writing; no reasonable time; a member the caller could not state
#ASSERT `s 137X(1) the trustee may require the unitholder to give the information` FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137X(1) the trustee may require the unitholder to give the information` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137X(1) the trustee may require the unitholder to give the information` TRUE NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137X(1) the trustee may require the unitholder to give the information` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137X(1) the trustee may require the unitholder to give the information` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b): only a member who holds the units as trustee; a member who does not is outside the "if", and the function is named for a power, so the answer is NOTHING (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; the other reading is JUST FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 137X(1)(b) the trustee may require the unitholder who holds the units as trustee to indicate the persons for whom the unitholder holds them` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137X(1)(b) the trustee may require the unitholder who holds the units as trustee to indicate the persons for whom the unitholder holds them` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137X(1)(b) the trustee may require the unitholder who holds the units as trustee to indicate the persons for whom the unitholder holds them` FALSE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 137X(2): a further notice (a gated power, split site (ii), both readings)`
#ASSERT `s 137X(2) the trustee may require the other person to give the information` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137X(2)(a) the trustee may require the other person to inform it whether the person holds the interest as beneficial owner or as trustee` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the trustee has not been informed that the person has an interest: not covered (the grant reading), where the "where" reading would say no
#ASSERT `s 137X(2) the trustee may require the other person to give the information` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137X(2) the trustee may require the other person to give the information` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137X(2)(b) the trustee may require the other person who holds the interest as trustee to indicate the persons for whom it is held` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137X(2)(b) the trustee may require the other person who holds the interest as trustee to indicate the persons for whom it is held` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 137X(3): control of voting rights by agreement or arrangement`
#ASSERT `s 137X(3) the trustee may require the unitholder to inform it whether the voting rights are subject to an agreement or arrangement` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137X(3) the trustee may require the unitholder to inform it whether the voting rights are subject to an agreement or arrangement` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- particulars only "if so"; no agreement or arrangement is outside the "if" and the answer is NOTHING (the grant ruling, limit 1)
#ASSERT `s 137X(3) the trustee may require the unitholder to give particulars of the agreement or arrangement and the parties to it` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137X(3) the trustee may require the unitholder to give particulars of the agreement or arrangement and the parties to it` TRUE (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 137X(4) to (7): the notice's content, the duty to comply, the register`
#ASSERT `s 137X(4) the notice contains the other information the Authority prescribes and is delivered as it prescribes` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137X(4) the notice contains the other information the Authority prescribes and is delivered as it prescribes` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137X(4) the notice contains the other information the Authority prescribes and is delivered as it prescribes` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 137X(5) the person must comply with the notice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no notice issued to the person: "Any person to whom a notice is issued" says nothing about this person
#ASSERT `s 137X(5) the person must comply with the notice` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the notice allows 5 days: an answer on day 5 is in time, on day 6 not
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 137X(5) the person must comply with the notice within the time it specifies` (Individual "the unitholder") 5 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "the unitholder" DOES `s 137X comply with the notice` AT 5
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 137X(5) the person must comply with the notice within the time it specifies` (Individual "the unitholder") 5 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "the unitholder" DOES `s 137X comply with the notice` AT 6
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 137X(5) the person must comply with the notice within the time it specifies` (Individual "the unitholder") 5 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)
-- (6): "Whenever" counts as "where": no information received, the text's no
#ASSERT `s 137X(6) the trustee must inscribe the fact of the requirement, its date and the information in a separate part of the register` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137X(6) the trustee must inscribe the fact of the requirement, its date and the information in a separate part of the register` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 137X(6) the trustee must inscribe the fact of the requirement, its date and the information in a separate part of the register` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 137X(7) section 137V applies to the separate part of the register` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 137X(7) section 137V applies to the separate part of the register` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 137X(8) to (11): offences, the defence and the bar`
-- split site (i), both readings, as in section 137D
